<h2><center>Task 4A: Problem Statement</center></h2>
<hr>

## Objective

After navigating through the storm-scattered crates, DharaBot now reaches the narrow lakeside passage that runs along the edge of the farm. The heavy rain has caused the nearby lake to overflow, flooding one side of the path and pushing loose soil against the high wall on the other. Now, DharaBot must rely on its proximity sensors to stay perfectly aligned with the wall, because one wrong move could send it crashing through the walls into the water! Help DharaBot follow the curve of the wall with steady precision and escape safely.


The theme for this task is "Controllers".
We will learn about bang-bang controllers and design a controller to follow the walls in the arena by using inputs from the distance sensors. <br>
The aim of the task is to reach the other end of the arena while collecting all the waypoints and avoiding collision with the walls. When the simulation starts, a timer of 180 seconds will automatically start. A new waypoint will appear everytime when the robot collects a waypoint till the robot reaches the other end of the arena. The timer will stop either when the robot reaches the other end of the arena or when the robot collides with a wall.

